{
 "version": 1,
 "notes": [
  "The provider configuration (IR-01, IR-02, SR-05). A client sends a request only to a host on the allowlist, and the allowlist is here and in no other place. No user interface and no scenario file can set a provider address (SR-05).",
  "The local endpoint is the llama.cpp server on the owner's network: four hosts with one model each, and the owner's workstation as the fifth (`local5`, 172.20.1.174, with the Q6_K file because its card holds 32 GB). SR-05 names the local endpoint as the one private-network exception, and the five hosts are that endpoint. The loopback address stays off the list. The name `local*` in an agent name is the pool of them: a game takes the host its worker is bound to, or the host its seed names, and the others are its failover.",
  "A `request` field holds the fields the adapter adds to each request of that provider. The local rows turn the thinking of Qwen3 off, because the harness asks for a short analysis and a JSON object, and a thinking pass spends thousands of hidden tokens first.",
  "A provider with no key on the machine is unavailable, and a run says so and goes on (SR-02)."
 ],
